110 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 336 0 R
/T (Kernel Resource Exhaustion: High-volume UDP DNS query floods saturate Linux servers because the kernel wastes massive CPU cycles allocating socket buffers \(sk_buff\) before malicious packets ever reach user-space daemons or firewalls.)
/E (Kernel Resource Exhaustion: High-volume UDP DNS query floods saturate Linux servers because the kernel wastes massive CPU cycles allocating socket buffers \(sk_buff\) before malicious packets ever reach user-space daemons or firewalls.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
111 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 337 0 R
/T (Inefficiency of Traditional Filtering: Standard Netfilter and nftables firewalls inspect packets too late in the networking pipeline, resulting in heavy context-switching overhead and packet queue drops under high packet-per-second \(pps\) loads.)
/E (Inefficiency of Traditional Filtering: Standard Netfilter and nftables firewalls inspect packets too late in the networking pipeline, resulting in heavy context-switching overhead and packet queue drops under high packet-per-second \(pps\) loads.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
112 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 338 0 R
/T (Legitimate Service Disruption: Server CPU starvation and queue exhaustion cause legitimate user DNS queries to experience severe timeouts or complete denial of service during volumetric floods. )
/E (Legitimate Service Disruption: Server CPU starvation and queue exhaustion cause legitimate user DNS queries to experience severe timeouts or complete denial of service during volumetric floods. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 339 0 R
/T (Project Objective: Implement an in-kernel eBPF/XDP rate limiter directly inside the network interface driver to parse UDP/DNS queries and enforce bounded per-source and global rate limits before kernel memory allocation occurs. )
/E (Project Objective: Implement an in-kernel eBPF/XDP rate limiter directly inside the network interface driver to parse UDP/DNS queries and enforce bounded per-source and global rate limits before kernel memory allocation occurs. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 340 0 R
/T (Empirical Benchmarking: Measure and validate the mitigation efficiency \(throughput, CPU utilization, drop rate, and legitimate query success\) across three synthetic load scenarios against both nftables and no-filter baselines in an isolated host pair.)
/E (Empirical Benchmarking: Measure and validate the mitigation efficiency \(throughput, CPU utilization, drop rate, and legitimate query success\) across three synthetic load scenarios against both nftables and no-filter baselines in an isolated host pair.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
