120 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 89 0 R
/T (The Domain Name System \(DNS\) relies extensively on connectionless UDP traffic, making it a frequent target for high-rate, spoofed volumetric attacks. In standard Linux networking architectures, the operating system kernel processes incoming packets by allocating memory for socket buffers \(sk_buff\) before routing them to user-space applications or traditional firewalls.)
/E (The Domain Name System \(DNS\) relies extensively on connectionless UDP traffic, making it a frequent target for high-rate, spoofed volumetric attacks. In standard Linux networking architectures, the operating system kernel processes incoming packets by allocating memory for socket buffers \(sk_buff\) before routing them to user-space applications or traditional firewalls.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
