/T (NIC Driver Level Processing: Intercepts UDP/DNS traffic directly at the network interface driver level \(XDP hook\), dropping malicious packets before the Linux kernel spends CPU cycles allocating socket buffers \(sk_buff\) or triggering context switches.)
/E (NIC Driver Level Processing: Intercepts UDP/DNS traffic directly at the network interface driver level \(XDP hook\), dropping malicious packets before the Linux kernel spends CPU cycles allocating socket buffers \(sk_buff\) or triggering context switches.)
