492 0 obj
<<
/Title (Inefficiency of Traditional Filtering: Standard Netfilter and nftables firewalls inspect packets too late in the networking pipeline, resulting in heavy context-switching overhead and packet queue drops under high packet-per-second \(pps\) loads.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 211 0 R
/Prev 380 0 R
/Next 585 0 R
>>
endobj
493 0 obj
<<
/Title (Project Objective: Implement an in-kernel eBPF/XDP rate limiter directly inside the network interface driver to parse UDP/DNS queries and enforce bounded per-source and global rate limits before kernel memory allocation occurs.)
/Dest [11 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 211 0 R
/Prev 585 0 R
/Next 381 0 R
>>
endobj
494 0 obj
<<
/Title (AIORI 3)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 381 0 R
/First 586 0 R
/Last 586 0 R
/Count -1
>>
endobj
495 0 obj
<<
/Title (The Domain Name System \(DNS\) relies extensively on connectionless UDP traffic, making it a frequent target for high-rate, spoofed volumetric attacks. In standard Linux networking architectures, the operating system kernel processes incoming packets by allocating memory for socket buffers \(sk_buff\) before routing them to user-space applications or traditional firewalls.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 382 0 R
/Next 496 0 R
>>
endobj
