/Title (RFC 1035 \(Domain Names - Implementation and Specification\): Defines the strict structural format of DNS messages over UDP \(Port 53\). Understanding these fixed header boundaries is essential for implementing the bounded UDP/DNS packet parsing required by the eBPF verifier, allowing safe extraction of identifiers without requiring full semantic parsing.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 497 0 R
/Next 639 0 R
>>
endobj
589 0 obj
<<
/Title (Netfilter vs. XDP Performance Studies: Existing literature on Linux networking performance highlights the limitations of standard nftables firewalls under high-volume load, specifically the CPU exhaustion caused by sk_buff memory allocation. In contrast, eBPF documentation and recent XDP proposals establish the network interface driver-level execution model as the modern standard for line-rate packet dropping and efficient DDoS mitigation.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 497 0 R
/Prev 639 0 R
/First 640 0 R
/Last 640 0 R
/Count -1
