641 0 obj
<<
/Title (We propose an in-kernel rate limiter running at the network interface driver level via eBPF and XDP. It inspects incoming packets before the Linux kernel allocates socket buffers \(sk_buff\), preventing CPU starvation during volumetric attacks.)
/Dest [14 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 590 0 R
/Next 651 0 R
>>
